ng the AdaLN parameter set is dynamic activations broadcast, not static weights. My next step is to recompute these on-the-fly within the kernel to eliminate significant CPU-side overhead and reduce memory footprint.\n\n**Streaming Fixed Weights**\n\nMy understanding has shifted; the 24.2 GiB AdaLN parameter set represents fixed weights, not dynamic activations. These weights, comprising 496 MiB per block across 50 layers, must be streamed. I'm integrating them into the existing SSD streaming buffer system to manage VRAM constraints and reduce PCIe thrashing.\n\n**Integrating Fixed Weights**\n\nMy latest realization is that the 24.2 GiB AdaLN parameters are fixed weights. I'm now integrating these into the SSD streaming system, utilizing the two 2.5 GiB slots, to avoid retaining them in shared memory and manage VRAM effectively.\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3364,"completion_tokens":6615,"total_tokens":9979,"cost":0.086108,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.086108,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.006728,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.07938},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":4196,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}
